 "admission_rule": {
  "standing": "SECONDARY label views, reported beside the primary, never a frame change",
  "primary": {
   "vm": "L6, the six-season label (efv_dataset._label_6yr), censored tail projected at the observed rate, weight observed_seasons / 6",
   "lv": "W3 (efv_labels.labels_for), WAR over the first three seasons, 0 if no debut in V..V+3"
  },
  "rules": [
   "A secondary view is reported beside the primary in the same table, with its own n, its own floor from the same resampler, and the word SECONDARY; it never replaces the primary before a reserved read, and no ship decision, weight, order or claim reads it.",
   "A view enters the screening lab (EFV3_B1) as a label family 'label_view' with members first3 and first4: the candidate arm is the base assembly scored against the view instead of the primary, on the same development folds, with the same statistic, the same noise-column floors and its own Holm family; it admits nothing to the assembly.",
   "A view enters the matrix (EFV3_D1 / D2) as a LABEL-VIEW axis beside the outcome thresholds (1, 2, 3, 4 career WAR): every cell declares which label it was scored against, and a cell on a secondary view carries the word SECONDARY and its target-validity note.",
   "Target validity is stated plainly wherever a view is printed: the industry FV frame is six-year value (the five FanGraphs FV-to-WAR tables, the Clemens kernel and the served grade are all six-season quantities), so a first-k view measures a different quantity, and its gain is rows resolved without projection, not accuracy.",
   "On a reserved frame a view is read only by the look that owns the frame, in the same run, as a secondary row; a view never opens a reserved frame on its own.",
   "The 2026 season is a label season only after the epoch's step D+U moves RESOLVED_THROUGH; before that no view reads a 2025 or 2026 line (this tool reads through 2024)."
  ]
 },
